 all right so what's next gosh  that's so amazing um well i guess what  was next was top boy let's talk about  that how did that work come about in  particular wow um that was insane so um  i remember i got a phone call um from  dez hamilton  um saying that he wanted to see me for  top way so  i was super duper excited um got in the  space i think overall i had maybe four  auditions three recalls  in total and so i had my first audition  and i had three recalls after that  um and it was a bit of a long process  i'm not gonna lie you know sometimes you  know when you don't hear from jobs  you're like oh yeah no i haven't got it  it's all right better luck next time  um so i just kind of took it on the chin  really and then  i think it was like every month i was  getting a call back and i've thinking  wow what is going on they're really  taking their time here um  and then yeah i got a phone call one day  saying that i had bagged the job and i  was in the middle of washing my hair  proper old school got my head over the  bath with the shower go in for it and  i'm flinging shampoo and came literally  all over the bathroom as soon as i found  out that i bagged the job oh my god  that's so funny that's it she just  reminded me of when i got my phone call  saying that i'd got my formerly  presenting gig and literally being in  the middle of my bed halfway through and  up i swear these calls always come at  the most random times um and then having  to like act composed and as if i didn't  just wake up 10 seconds ago um but for  people that are watching this who you  know are still grafting they're still in  the process of you know hopefully  getting that phone call and going to  auditions what advice would you give to  them to make themselves stand out and  hopefully seize those opportunities  especially from an acting point of view  well first things first when it comes  down to casting directors and auditions  and things like that i would say  100 make sure that you're prepared  you know when you walk into that  audition space you need to know your  script you know and sometimes they say  oh we don't need you to be off book be  off book  be be the person that is different from  everybody else because now people have  seen that they don't need to be off book  some of them aren't really going to  bother you know be the person that  stands out be yourself have fun with it  you know if you show people that you're  being yourself and you're able to have  fun and you're flamboyant and all of  these different things you know and you  can take a script and turn it into your  own  you know that's what you need to be  doing have fun with it play about you  know and always leave a good lasting  impression because they will always call  you back one thing i pride myself in is  kind of not caring and this is something  that  maggie from the big house and her  company maggie norrish is  um but she was my mentor for a long long  time and i used to struggle with  kind of  how can i explain it i would say i'm  more worried about what other people  would think so when it comes down to  some parts in the script i'm like oh no  i'm not doing that it sounds silly you  know i'm always worried about how i'm  being perceived or something like that  and she just got me just you know let go  and not care about that and stop saying  things like i can't oh no my yeah i  can't do this i can't i can't i can't  there's no such thing as i can't  you can  you can try and if it doesn't work you  try a different way i feel like that  mindset in general in this industry is  so important because throughout your  career you can face so many different  obstacles but if you approach it with  that i can mindset then literally  anything is possible um it's something  which i always like to share over on my  youtube channel to my audience um as  it's something which i just believe is  so so powerful um and yeah it's amazing  that she was able to share that  knowledge with you and i guess nicely  leads me onto the topic of role models  actually um how important would you say  role models are with your career  and who are your role models in the  acting industry oh gosh i've got so many  that's what i'm saying i've got so many  inspirations from role models for me  it's definitely gotta be denzel  washington  he's absolutely amazing  um idris elba absolutely amazing big big  legend every role model has their own  little things  i mean it's like one piece from here one  piece from here one piece from here so  you know i would say it's a good thing  to have loads of role models or at least  like you know maybe five to ten that you  can look up to because then you can take  a little bit from everybody ah cause  that's what i like to do as well just  take as much in from everyone and then  like tailor it into your own path um but  jasmine you're obviously such a huge  role model for so many people out there  um so to everyone who's watching who  wants to be in your shoes and be an  actress or an actor um what advice do  you give and like practical steps that  they can do to make that a reality well  i would 110 recommend finding somewhere  that do acting workshops or something  like that  um i would also recommend possibly  getting involved in like writing  projects one of my friends right now was  actually doing a writing project which  is an intensive 12-week course i believe  um but she's absolutely amazing she's  also upcoming actress too  um so yeah i would say just just make  sure you're always keeping yourself busy  you know and in fact nowadays there's so  much going on you know you've got people  that are doing their youtube podcasts  and things like that you know so it's  like you could even possibly i don't  know create something with a group of  friends you know and film it and all  that kind of stuff create your own short  films play about improvise all that kind  of stuff you know so like  it's endless what you could do with y